- This might be the only chance [br] I'll get to ask her about what [br] else she did in Scotland.
	Lizzy: so, when you were taking your uh, gap years, what else did you get up to?
	Lizzy: any whacky adventures?
	Valerie: hm.
	Valerie: well, there was that coven I joined for a short time.
	Valerie: they were quite fun.
	Lizzy: you joined a coven??
	Valerie: yes, they were all the rage back then.
	Valerie: of course, having knowledge of the supernatural helped me find legitimate ones over the more metaphorical.
	Lizzy: that's awesome!
	Lizzy: did you guys cast spells and eat hearts for power?
	Valerie: spells, yes. Hearts...
	Valerie: not really.
	Lizzy: not really isn't a no.
	Valerie: it's more nuanced.
	Lizzy: well, okay, what type of spells did you cast.
	Valerie: mostly good luck charms and curses.
	Lizzy: curses?
	Lizzy: who were you cursing.
	Valerie: a wide variety.
	Valerie: I'm not entirely proud of who was in my early twenties,
	Valerie: but I can't deny I was very good at making people regret crossing me.
	Lizzy: you just became two hundred percent cooler.
	Lizzy: is there any chance you could cast a spell right now?
	Valerie: I'm sorry, Elizabeth, but unfortunately I no longer possess the ability.
	Valerie: I've been out of practice for far too long.
	Valerie: and I'd rather not give in to the temptation.
	Lizzy: it was worth a shot.
- 
	Lizzy: so.
	Lizzy: you grew up in the Keep, right?
	Valerie: that's correct.
	Lizzy: what was that like?
	Lizzy: i only found out about paranormal stuff being real when I was turned into a werewolf,
	Lizzy: but you've known your whole life!
	Valerie: there is a certain madness in keeping a secret such as that, but I suppose that's why my order is called the Keepers.
	Valerie: it's not entirely lonely, however.
	Valerie: my mother was told when she married my father, and once they had children, the information was shared with us.
	Valerie: and the Keep has plenty of families within it.
	Valerie: families in which we can mingle and form close bonds.
	Lizzy: like arranged marriage?
	Valerie: er,
	Valerie: i don't like thinking about it like that,
	Valerie: the Keepers prefer to keep it within the order, but marriage and relationships outside of the keep is also permitted.
	Valerie: are you interested in joining the order?
	Valerie: im not sure how they'd feel about,
	Valerie: a... um...
	Lizzy: werewolf?
	Valerie: american.
	Lizzy: oh. Well.
	Lizzy: I'm not interested in joining, so you don't have to worry about that.
	Valerie: hm, that's a shame. You would make an excellent keeper.
	Valerie: if you change your mind, when we figure out a way to stop this whole thing, please let me know.
	Lizzy: thanks, VAL.
